==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{clipping|en|technology}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛknoʊ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|music genre}} A [[repetitive]] style of [[music]] originally produced for use in a continuous DJ set. The central rhythmic component is most often in common time (4/4), where time is marked with a bass drum on each quarter note pulse, a backbeat played by snare or clap on the second and fourth pulses of the bar, and an open hi-hat sounding every second eighth note.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|technopop}}
* {{l|en|technorock}}

